{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe \"O_EXCL-create a lock file, write a v2 owner stamp, reclaim once if stale\" loop exists **three**\ntimes, not twice:\n\n- `llm/enrich_drain.py:98-170` `_acquire_advisory_lock` (73) / `:173-178` `_release_advisory_lock`\n- `_commands/compact_trigger.py:119-160` `_acquire_trigger_lock` (42) / `:163-173` `release_trigger_lock`\n- `_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:109-145` `_acquire_worker_lock` (37) / `:148-158` `release_worker_lock`\n\nEach opens `os.open(path, os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY, 0o644)` inside `for attempt in\nrange(2)`, adjudicates with `rebar._store.lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale(path)`, unlinks and\nretries once on a stale verdict, then writes `lock_owner._owner_stamp()`. The copy spread the\nunresolved-path defect (`nuclear-calm-heron` = `da68-fc7c-068c-4c53`, closed) and was called a third\ndialect by `knavish-stimulated-bluebottle` (`aadc-9af6-0e67-4e2a`, closed). Dependency\n`6f18-05de-beaf-42be` (closed) landed: all three derive paths from `StorePaths`/`_gc_dir`; no `_rebar_dir` helper remains.\n\n### The copies are NOT identical\n1. **Same:** the ceiling (all call `stamped_file_is_stale(path)` bare; sole ceiling\n   `_MKDIR_LOCK_STALE_CEILING_S = 3600`, `lock_owner.py:46`) and the retry cap `range(2)`.\n2. **Release semantics — the one real behaviour delta; FIX it, do not propagate it.**\n   `_release_advisory_lock` (`enrich_drain.py:174-178`) wraps `os.close(fd)` and `os.unlink(...)` in\n   ONE `try`, so an `OSError` from `close` SKIPS the unlink and leaks the lock until the ceiling. `release_trigger_lock` (`compact_trigger.py:164-173`) and `release_worker_lock`\n   (`gc_trigger.py:149-158`) use TWO independent `try` blocks, so the unlink always runs. **The\n   shared implementation MUST use the two-block form** — a deliberate, tested change to the drain.\n3. **Stamp bytes.** Drain appends `\"\\n\"` (`enrich_drain.py:165`), the others do not\n   (`compact_trigger.py:156`, `gc_trigger.py:142`) — invisible, both readers `.read().strip()`\n   (`lock_owner.py:349-350`, `doctor_locks.py:279-280`). Adopt no-newline.\n4. **Logging.** Drain names the holder via `_describe_drain_lock_holder`\n   (`enrich_drain.py:129-134`, helper `:74-95`) and warns on a failed stamp (`:167-169`); the others\n   log bare (`compact_trigger.py:147`, `gc_trigger.py:132`) and swallow the stamp failure. The\n   drain's holder phrasing is pinned to `doctor`'s wording by\n   `test_enrich_drain.py:585::test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically` and\n   **must survive**. Adopt the drain's stamp-failure WARNING everywhere (logging superset).\n\n## Approach\nExtract `src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py` beside `lock_owner.py`, which stays the staleness\nauthority (the new module has no staleness logic of its own):\n- `stamped_file_lock(path, *, label, describe_holder=None) -> int | None` — O_EXCL create, stamp\n  write, single stale-reclaim, reclaim WARNING (drain passes `_describe_drain_lock_holder`, the\n  other two `None`), stamp-failure WARNING, and the ACCEPTED RACE comment moved verbatim from\n  `enrich_drain.py:135-163` (operator decision 2026-08-16 — a ruling that must not be dropped).\n- `release_stamped_lock(path, fd) -> None` — the **two-independent-`try`** close+unlink.\n\n**Directory creation stays with the callers** — the mechanisms differ: drain and compaction\n`os.makedirs(StorePaths(tracker).rebar_dir, exist_ok=True)` returning `None` on `OSError`\n(`enrich_drain.py:118-122`, `compact_trigger.py:135-139`); GC uses `_gc_dir`'s\n`mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` (`gc_trigger.py:65-69,122-125`). The helper takes a resolved\n`path: str | os.PathLike[str]` (GC passes `Path`).\n\n**Guard anchor: `os.O_CREAT` ∧ `stamped_file_is_stale`, NOT `O_EXCL`.** A bare `O_EXCL` scan\nover-matches 7 legitimate lines (`_signing_hmac.py:100,104`, `_store/fsutil.py:13`,\n`opcert_service/keyprov.py:122`, `llm/code_review/registry.py:385`, `doctor_locks.py:49,249`), and\n`O_EXCL` ∧ `stamped_file_is_stale` still matches `doctor_locks.py` — the diagnostic READER (real\ncall `:304`, opens WITHOUT `O_CREAT` at `:119`).\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner\nmodule exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition\ncount where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour\npinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Constraints\n- `compact_trigger._acquire_trigger_lock` and `release_trigger_lock` are monkeypatched **by name as\n  module attributes** at `tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py:134-135` with **no\n  `raising=False`** — both must stay module-level attributes of `rebar._commands.compact_trigger`\n  or that test errors. They and `gc_trigger.release_worker_lock` are PUBLIC; no renames. All six\n  are called directly by the three worker test modules.\n- `doctor_locks` reads these stamps (`:101-103`, `_existence_report` `:248-317`, `scan_locks`\n  `:320-370`): stamp bytes must stay `.strip()`-equivalent.\n- `compact_trigger.maybe_compact:302-306` acquires then immediately releases as a **detection\n  probe**, not exclusion — the helper must stay cheap and side-effect-free beyond the file. Other\n  call sites: `drain` `:328`/`:376`; `run_sweep` `:223`/`:265`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py` (new), `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py`,\n`tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nNew tests: acquire / second refused / release / re-acquire; a stale stamp\n(`monkeypatch.setattr(lock_owner, \"_pid_alive\", lambda _pid: False)`) reclaimed exactly once, third\ncollision `None`, live stamp never reclaimed; stamp parity; release-on-close-failure; the drain's\nholder WARNING. The pinning suites named in the Acceptance Criteria are green today (80 passed).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No `src/rebar` module outside `stamped_lock.py` performs the acquire; checked by\n  `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py -q` and by\n  `grep -rlF \"os.O_CREAT\" src/rebar --include=\"*.py\" | xargs grep -lF \"stamped_file_is_stale\" | grep -v \"^src/rebar/_store/stamped_lock.py$\"`\n  printing nothing. Today it prints exactly the three files listed above.\n- [ ] The unrelated `O_EXCL` uses survive; checked by\n  `grep -c \"O_EXCL\" src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`\n  still totalling its current 7 matches.\n- [ ] The six lock functions still exist as module attributes with unchanged signatures; checked by\n  `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py tests/unit/test_lock_age_ceiling.py tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py -q`, which also pins concurrent refusal and single reclaim for all three workers.\n- [ ] The shared stamp is `.strip()`-equal to `lock_owner._owner_stamp()` and\n  `doctor_locks._existence_report` resolves a holder from a lock made through it; checked by\n  `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py` (absent today, so that pytest errors now).\n- [ ] Releasing a lock whose `os.close` raises still unlinks the file — the two-`try` form fixing\n  `enrich_drain.py:174-178`; checked by\n  `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py::test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails`.\n- [ ] The drain's reclaim WARNING still names the holder; checked by `.venv/bin/python -m pytest\n  \"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py::test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically\"`.\n- [ ] Net non-test LOC is negative; checked by\n  `git show --numstat HEAD -- src/rebar | awk '{a+=$1; d+=$2} END {print a-d}'` printing < 0."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787371013242566001,"uuid":"c369f3f2-9cf3-4080-a596-ffdabfafdfc7"}